face-image: img/Kollwitz_Arbeitslosigkeit.jpg

= Unemployment Insurance Crisis

The economic crisis has caused mass layoffs all throughout Germany, affecting the industrial working class the hardest. Welfare spending is increasing due to the greater need.

Predictably, the Grand Coalition is on the verge of collapse. The industrial backers of the Center and DVP support we4lfare cuts while the SPD opposes them



- @groko_collapse: The Grand Coalition collapses!

@groko_collapse
call: set_next_election_time
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 0; z_relation -= 8; dvp_relation -= 10; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z "; welfare -= 2; budget += 1; inflation -= 2; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = ddp_name; finance_minister_party = "DVP"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; spd_no_confidence = 1; pro_republic -= 4; old_middle_spd -= 3; new_middle_spd -= 2; rural_spd -= 2; catholics_spd -= 2; economic_growth -= 0.6

Predictably, the colaition falls apart. Heinrich Brüning of the Center Party has been appointed Chancellor. With an all-bourgeois cabinet.  Brüning and President Hindenburg use the emergency powers of article 48 to cut welfare, bypassing The Reichstag entirely. This trend towards dictatorial bourgeois does not bode well for us...